**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** One spelling per kit folder, so the kit history and the one-window-per-kit rule (step 190) name a kit the same way (001 §E 'Concurrency: one window per kit'; 001 §F: the history holds one entry per folder; step 164: a kit is identified by its folder, compared ignoring case by one private member of `KitHistory`; .spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call'). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`, on `KitFolder` (step 122) beside `tryKitPathOf` (step 132), its doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3: `member this.canonical : KitFolder` answers the folder's text with every backslash turned into `/`, every trailing `/` removed and the rest upper-cased (`ToUpperInvariant`), so the folder written `C:\kits\Optics QZ\` and the folder written `c:/KITS/optics qz` answer one `KitFolder`. It touches no disk and resolves no relative path. It is a key, never a path to show or open: the history and the windows keep showing a folder as the user chose it. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs`: the private folder comparison of `KitHistory` (step 164) compares the two folders' `canonical`s, and its `StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase` text comparison is deleted, so one rule decides when two folders are one kit. `star`, `unstar`, `forget`, `bump` (step 169) and `relocate` (step 171) keep their code and reach it through that member. No other member, cache or option is added. Tests. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs` (step 122) gains `two spellings of one kit folder share one canonical form`: the folders written `C:\kits\Optics QZ\` (backslashes, a trailing one), `C:/kits/Optics QZ` and `c:/KITS/optics qz/` answer equal `canonical`s, each equal to `KitFolder (FolderName "C:/KITS/OPTICS QZ")`, and `C:/kits/Optics QY` answers another. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs` (step 164) gains `a kit is matched by its folder in any spelling`: over step 164's `mixed` history, `star` of the folder written `C:\Kits\A\` stars `a` and leaves every other entry, the stored order and every time unchanged, and `forget` of `c:/kits/b/` removes `b` alone. Every earlier `KitHistoryTests` and `KitHistoryProxyTests` fact keeps its assertions.

**Acceptance.** After the canonical form lands, `KitFolder.canonical` MUST answer one folder for every spelling of a path and `KitHistory` MUST match folders through it; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `two spellings of one kit folder share one canonical form` and `a kit is matched by its folder in any spelling`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.
